$NetBSD$

Origin: EmberBSD contributors (AI-assisted), adapted from Ryo ONODERA's
pkgsrc-wip change 416bbac2b9ed6f3eb729dfa1a2f1c5221ff6bd3e:
https://mail-index.netbsd.org/pkgsrc-wip-changes/2026/09/09/msg037649.html
Retain upstream MIT licensing. Not submitted upstream.

NetBSD/amd64 rtld has no TLSDESC relocation support. An executable probe can
relax TLS accesses and accept a dialect that a shared library cannot use.
Extend the upstream FreeBSD guard only to the affected NetBSD architecture.
Keep compiler defaults, the cross execution guard and other targets unchanged.

--- meson.build.orig
+++ meson.build
@@ -637,8 +637,11 @@
   # cross-compiling, but because this is just an optimization we can skip it
   if meson.is_cross_build() and not meson.can_run_host_binaries()
     warning('cannot auto-detect -mtls-dialect when cross-compiling, using compiler default')
-  elif host_machine.system() == 'freebsd'
-    warning('cannot use -mtls-dialect for FreeBSD, using compiler default')
+  # NetBSD/amd64 rtld cannot process TLSDESC relocations in shared libraries.
+  # Executable TLS relaxation can hide this requirement from the run probe.
+  elif host_machine.system() == 'freebsd' or (
+    host_machine.system() == 'netbsd' and host_machine.cpu_family() == 'x86_64')
+    warning('cannot auto-select -mtls-dialect for this target, using compiler default')
   else
     # The way to specify the TLSDESC dialect is architecture-specific.
     # We probe both because there is not a fallback guaranteed to work for all
